  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection of Threatened Sumatran Ape Populations and Their Habitats, and Mitigation of the Impact of Road Expansion Within Bukit Barisan Selatan National Park</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to prevent habitat loss for gibbons and siamangs through patrols with park rangers especially near roads in areas under high threat of deforestation, support park authorities to understand the impacts of road expansion based on analysis of longitudinal studies on the population and distribution of siamang and gibbon in BBS, and use this to develop recommendations for mitigating road development impacts, and reduce poaching and trafficking of apes through targeting key poaching and wildlife trade networks in and around BBS. Project will support SMART patrols in key areas in the national park, complete analysis of gibbon/siamang data to understand impacts of road expansion, and reduce poaching and trafficking of apes.</narrative>
  </description>
